# TEMPORARY, and NARROWED 2026-07-24: only WORKFLOWS are unpushable, not all of `.github/`.
#
# The reason is a credential, not a policy: the local gh token lacks the `workflow` scope, so a push that
# touches `.github/workflows/*` is rejected outright. That is why this ignore exists. But it was written as
# `.github/`, which silently swallowed the whole directory — and the first thing that cost us was CODEOWNERS:
# `main`'s ruleset requires a code-owner review, no CODEOWNERS file could be committed, so the requirement
# could not be satisfied and a finished PR sat blocked with no route through it.
#
# So: ignore the directory that actually has the restriction, and nothing else.
#
# NOTE for whoever lands CI (Sean, 2026-07-24): `.github/workflows/ci.yml` exists ON DISK, untracked, from
# 2026-07-08 — and it is STALE. It sets `working-directory: greenfield-engine`, which no longer exists (the
# project is `integrity-engine` now), so it would fail as written. Treat it as a starting point at best.
# A push from an account whose token HAS the `workflow` scope can commit workflows normally; this ignore is
# only working around this machine's credential.
.github/workflows/

# Monorepo root ignores (OS / editor). Project-specific ignores live in each project's .gitignore.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Claude Code — MACHINE-LOCAL ONLY. Deliberately NOT a blanket `.claude/` ignore: shared config
# (settings.json, skills/, commands/, agents/) is useful to anyone working on this repo with Claude
# and SHOULD stay committable. Only the two machine-specific things are excluded:
#   • worktrees/ are full recursive checkouts of this repo inside itself, complete with build
#     artifacts. They are untracked, so a stray `git add -A` from the main checkout would stage the
#     lot — this ignore is the guard against that.
#   • settings.local.json is per-machine by Claude Code's own `.local.` convention (an accumulated
#     Bash permission allowlist); on a PUBLIC repo it can also leak local paths and service names.
# Neither is left unprotected: both are captured for disaster recovery by the PRIVATE infra repo
# (~/workspace/domain_management/backup-infra.sh). Ignored here, backed up there.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
